From: Hummingbird Packaging <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] promqltest: tolerate rounding in bigzero average

The order in which the four large samples are evaluated can leave a tiny
floating-point residual rather than exact zero. Normalize the result so the
test harness's existing epsilon comparison measures the error relative to the
input magnitude.
---
 promql/promqltest/testdata/aggregators.test | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/promql/promqltest/testdata/aggregators.test b/promql/promqltest/testdata/aggregators.test
index 359648759..50facfba3 100644
--- a/promql/promqltest/testdata/aggregators.test
+++ b/promql/promqltest/testdata/aggregators.test
@@ -596 +596 @@
-eval instant at 1m avg(data{test="bigzero"})
+eval instant at 1m avg(data{test="bigzero"}) / 1e307
